From: 28allday
Subject: [PATCH] hwcontext_vulkan: enable VK_NV_optical_flow only when asked for

NVIDIA's driver loads and initialises CUDA when a device is created with
VK_NV_optical_flow, and CUDA then keeps the GPU out of runtime D3 until the
process exits, even after the device is destroyed. Programs that create a
device for encoding, never optical flow, kept a laptop's discrete GPU awake.
Enable it only when listed in the device_extensions option.
---
diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c
index 0ddfafb..0512096 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c
@@ -1013,6 +1013,14 @@ static int check_extensions(AVHWDeviceContext *ctx, int dev, AVDictionary *opts,
             !vulkan_device_has_rebar(ctx))
             continue;
 
+        /* NVIDIA's driver implements optical flow through CUDA: enabling it
+         * starts CUDA in the process, which then holds the GPU awake until
+         * the process ends, so a laptop's discrete GPU cannot power down
+         * after the device is gone. Only when asked for by name. */
+        if (dev && !strcmp(tstr, VK_NV_OPTICAL_FLOW_EXTENSION_NAME) &&
+            !(user_exts_str && strstr(user_exts_str, tstr)))
+            continue;
+
         if (dev &&
             ((debug_mode == FF_VULKAN_DEBUG_VALIDATE) ||
              (debug_mode == FF_VULKAN_DEBUG_PRINTF) ||
